# cmd.exe cannot parse a batch file whose blocks are delimited with bare LF: the body of
# every `if (...)` is silently skipped, so a launcher that "runs" and does nothing is the
# usual symptom. The committed blobs are LF, which is only turned into CRLF on checkout when
# the cloner happens to have core.autocrlf=true -- pin it instead of hoping.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# These are sourced by bash on the training side; a CR there breaks `set -a` / shebangs.
*.sh text eol=lf
